# Flowmark exclusions.
#
# POLICY: format the whole repository. Exclude only files we have a specific,
# tested reason to leave raw. Each exclusion below states that reason.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The literature archive: verbatim source and archival transcription.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Two independent reasons, both verified rather than assumed:
#
# 1. The *.raw.md files are unedited pdfminer output and serve as byte-level
#    ground truth for checking the model-assisted *.md transcriptions against.
#    Reflowing them voids that guarantee entirely.
#
# 2. The cleaned *.md transcriptions are transcribed text, and formatting them
#    would retype transcribed characters -- straight quotes, ellipses -- against
#    the rule that archived source is never edited to look tidy. Their inline
#    LaTeX is not the reason: the pinned flowmark-rs 0.4.0 keeps every $...$ span
#    in the archive whole, which `devtools.check_math_spans` re-measures on a copy.
#
# So the whole archive stays raw. Its README.md is NOT excluded -- it is our own
# prose and is formatted like everything else.
packing/resources/papers/
packing/resources/web/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated agent skill files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# These skill directories hold files carrying explicit DO-NOT-EDIT markers,
# regenerated byte-deterministically by their own tools (`tbd setup --auto`,
# `softschema skill --install`, `flowmark --install-skill`, `pprose install`).
# Formatting them would both diverge them from their generators and be silently
# overwritten on the next regeneration. The pprose skills bundle generated
# reference files beside their SKILL.md, so the whole directory is excluded.
#
# This is a category rule, not a per-file measured one: as of 2026-08-25 every
# file below is already flowmark-clean under the pinned version, so nothing here
# is drifting today. It is listed because we do not own these bytes — the
# generator does — and a future flowmark pin must not silently start rewriting
# them.
#
# Exclusion is per generated skill, NOT per skill directory: hand-written skills
# live alongside these and are formatted like all our other prose. Adding a
# generated skill means adding two lines here; adding a hand-written one means
# adding none.
.agents/skills/flowmark/
.agents/skills/pprose-common-edit/
.agents/skills/pprose-compare/
.agents/skills/pprose-copy-edit/
.agents/skills/pprose-de-slop/
